  <!-- Engineering Science Deep-Dive Section -->
  <div class="mb-10 bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8">
    <div class="mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">{d.scienceTitle}</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">{d.scienceSub}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">1. Micro-Channel Jet Kinematics &amp; Frontal Collision</h3>
        <p>
          Unlike conventional high-pressure valve homogenizers where fluid exits radially through a variable throttling slit, microfluidizers pass pressurized fluid through <strong>fixed-geometry diamond interaction chambers</strong>. In Y-type chambers, the feed stream bifurcates into two micro-channels (widths of 75 µm to 100 µm) that turn 90° and collide frontally at velocities governed by the Bernoulli orifice equation:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-white dark:bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl font-mono text-[11px] text-ink overflow-x-auto">
          v_jet = C_d &times; &radic;(2 &times; &Delta;P / &rho;) &nbsp;&approx;&nbsp; 0.92 &times; &radic;(2 &times; 150 &times; 10&sup6; / 1000) &approx; 504 m/s
        </div>
        <p>
          This frontal jet impingement generates extreme planar extensional strain rates (&epsilon;&#775; &gt; 10<sup>7</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>) and intense localized spatial energy dissipation rates (&epsilon; &gt; 10<sup>7</sup> - 10<sup>8</sup> W/kg) within the microscopic collision zone.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink mt-6">2. Kolmogorov Microscale &amp; Droplet Sizing Mechanics</h3>
        <p>
          Turbulent micro-eddy dissipation reduces droplet sizes according to the Kolmogorov micro-scale of turbulence:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-white dark:bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl font-mono text-[11px] text-ink overflow-x-auto">
          &eta; = (&nu;&sup3; / &epsilon;)<sup>1/4</sup> &nbsp;&approx;&nbsp; ((10<sup>-6</sup>)&sup3; / 10<sup>8</sup>)<sup>1/4</sup> &approx; 31.6 nm
        </div>
        <p>
          Because &eta; is smaller than the typical critical droplet diameter (D<sub>v50</sub> &approx; 40 - 80 nm), droplet breakup is governed by inertial turbulent shear and extensional flow. The resulting particle size distribution follows a narrow log-normal profile with a Polydispersity Index (PDI) below 0.12, ensuring thermodynamic stability against Ostwald ripening.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">3. Viscous Shear Dissipation &amp; In-Line Rapid Quench</h3>
        <p>
          Nearly 100% of the hydraulic mechanical energy delivered by the electro-hydraulic intensifier pump is converted into thermal energy through viscous dissipation inside the micro-channels. The adiabatic fluid temperature rise (&Delta;T) is calculated as:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-white dark:bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl font-mono text-[11px] text-ink overflow-x-auto">
          &Delta;T_adiabatic = &Delta;P / (&rho; &times; c_p) &nbsp;&approx;&nbsp; 150 &times; 10&sup6; / (1000 &times; 4184) &approx; +35.8&deg;C
        </div>
        <p>
          For temperature-sensitive lipophilic bioactives (such as Curcumin, Omega-3 DHA/EPA triglycerides, and Astaxanthin), prolonged exposure to temperatures above 45°C causes rapid lipid peroxidation and polyphenol degradation. Therefore, a <strong>sanitary shell-and-tube in-line glycol chiller</strong> must be plumbed directly downstream of the diamond interaction chamber to quench the fluid below 15°C in under 200 ms.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink mt-6">4. Ceramic Plunger Tribology &amp; Sanitary Compliance</h3>
        <p>
          Operating at continuous pressures up to 2,070 bar (30,000 psi) requires high-purity Yttria-Stabilized Tetragonal Zirconia Polycrystal (Y-TZP) ceramic plungers with Vickers hardness exceeding 13 GPa and mirror finishes (Ra &lt; 0.03 µm). Under 3-A Sanitary Standard 04-05 and EHEDG Doc 17, spring-energized virgin PTFE/UHMWPE seals prevent metal particle shedding and catastrophic high-pressure hydraulic fluid blow-by.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Engineering Specifications Data Table -->
  <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8">
